# StuWith line-ending and diff policy.
#
# `* text=auto` normalises line endings on commit, which is what `core.autocrlf`
# was doing per-clone. Stating it here makes it a property of the repository
# rather than of each developer machine.
#
# The second rule is the one with a story. `apps/api/src/auth/__testing__/auth-harness.ts`
# held a LITERAL NUL byte as a cookie-jar key separator, so git classified the
# central fixture of the login stories as BINARY: it showed in every diff as
# "Binary files differ", no reviewer could read it, and grep and ripgrep skipped
# it entirely — a source file no repo-wide check could see. Marking source as
# text means a stray NUL is a broken diff somebody notices, not a file that
# quietly leaves the review surface.

* text=auto

*.ts   text diff
*.tsx  text diff
*.js   text diff
*.mjs  text diff
*.cjs  text diff
*.json text diff
*.md   text diff
*.yml  text diff
*.yaml text diff
*.sql  text diff

